{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#4015","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#4015","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#4015\",\"parent_revision\":\"c56ecea533a4228ed238bb2ed09516bc81017387bff1e6d12470260d8ec2ae1a\",\"root_revision\":\"c56ecea533a4228ed238bb2ed09516bc81017387bff1e6d12470260d8ec2ae1a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: needs-grooming\\nadded: 2026-09-30\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nIn a Claude Code session isolated with EnterWorktree, the harness Bash guard refused `uv run plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/cli.py plan finish ... --result complete` (\\\"runs a string through complete\\\") \u2014 it reads the bare token `complete` as the shell builtin that executes a string. `plan finish --result complete` is the command dh:start-task tells every task worker to run to close an attempt, so no task can close normally in a worktree-isolated session. On #3978 task T0 attempt 2 a worker got around the guard by base64-decoding the word at runtime; auto mode flagged that as [Auto-Mode Bypass]. Implementation of #3978 is paused on this.\\n\\nImpact: blocks every dh implement-feature run in a worktree-isolated Claude Code session, and invites agents to obfuscate commands to get past a safety control.\\n\\nGoal (repo owner, 2026-09-30): \\\"adjust it to be unable to get the false positive in our code\\\" \u2014 no command the dh skills, agents or docs instruct an agent to run should contain a token the guard reads as a string-executing shell builtin.\\n\\nOther observed refusals in the same session (context, may or may not be in scope): a `for` loop over filenames containing \\\"github\\\"; a python heredoc that called `git rev-parse`.\\n\\nDuplicate check: the similarity check matched #3978, #3043, #3049, #3062, #3901; none concerns the Bash guard or plan finish.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session 2026-09-28/30: implementing #3978 (plan P999000ed) in an EnterWorktree-isolated session\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-30\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c9e849962b8e0f9fdb73f62aaabc19b2651a875b762dd2090bae0918046ea5c9\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABYDXP9w\",\"fields\":{\"stack\":\"\",\"status\":\"open\",\"item_type\":\"Bug\",\"priority\":\"P1\",\"added\":\"2026-09-30\",\"files\":\"\",\"followup_to\":\"\",\"layer\":\"\",\"research_first\":\"\",\"close_reference\":\"\",\"source\":\"Session 2026-09-28/30: implementing #3978 (plan P999000ed) in an EnterWorktree-isolated session\",\"groomed\":\"\",\"topic\":\"\",\"close_comment\":\"\",\"plan\":\"\",\"language\":\"\",\"suggested_location\":\"\",\"close_reason\":\"\"}}"}